.TH STUDWORX 1 "31 October 2026"
.SH NAME
StudWorx \- LDraw / LEGO\(rg model builder
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIstudworx \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIINFILE\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fIStudWorx \fR is a CAD program for creating virtual LEGO\(rg models. It
has an easy to use interface and includes thousands of different
parts in its library.
.PP
\fIINFILE\fR can be an LDraw model (.ldr, .mpd or .dat), or a LeoCAD
project (.lcd), which is read only and saved as LDraw. A LEGO\(rg Digital
Designer model (.lxf or .lxfml) is imported as an untitled project.

.SH OPTIONS
Below is a summary of all of the options that \fIStudWorx\fR
accepts. Many options have two equivalent names, one of
which is a single letter preceded by -, and the other of
which is a long name preceded by --. Brackets ([ and ])
indicate that an option takes an optional parameter.

.TP
.B infile
Loads the model file \fIinfile\fR

.TP
\fB\-l \fIpath\fR, \fB\-\-library \fIpath
.br
Set the parts library location.

.TP
\fB\-\-unofficial\-library \fIpath
.br
Set the LDraw unofficial parts archive, ldrawunf.zip next to the parts library by default.

.TP
\fB\-\-shadow\-library \fIpath
.br
Set the LDCad shadow library location, used to find connected parts.

.TP
\fB\-i \fR[\fIoutfile.ext\fR], \fB\-\-image \fR[\fIoutfile.ext\fR]
.br
Saves a picture to \fIoutfile.ext \fR in the image format specified
by \fIext\fR and exits. If outfile is not given then the program will
use a name based on \fIinfile\fR. The file format is selected by \fIext\fR
and can be png, jpg, bmp or gif, with one still GIF for each step (if \fIext\fR
is not present then the default preferences format will be used).
When a range of steps is saved, each picture gets its step number added
to the name, as in \fIoutfile01.png\fR.

.TP
\fB\-w \fIwidth\fR, \fB\-\-width \fIwidth
.br
Sets the width of the picture to \fIwidth\fR.

.TP
\fB\-\-height \fIheight
.br
Sets the height of the picture to \fIheight\fR.

.TP
\fB\-f \fIstep\fR, \fB\-\-from \fIstep
.br
Start saving pictures at the step \fIstep\fR. Steps start at 1 and end at 255.

.TP
\fB\-t \fIstep\fR, \fB\-\-to \fIstep
.br
Save pictures until the step \fIstep\fR.

.TP
\fB\-s \fIsubmodel\fR, \fB\-\-submodel \fIsubmodel
.br
Sets the active submodel to \fIsubmodel\fR.

.TP
\fB\-c \fIcamera\fR, \fB\-\-camera \fIcamera
.br
Sets the active camera to \fIcamera\fR.

.TP
\fB\-\-stud\-style\ \fIid
.br
Set the stud style. Valid values 0=Plain, 1=Thin-Line Logo, 2=Outline Logo, 3=Sharp Top Logo, 4=Rounded Top Logo, 5=Flattened Logo, 6=High Contrast, 7=High Contrast Logo.

.TP
\fB\-\-viewpoint \fRfront\ |\ back\ |\ left\ |\ right\ |\ top\ |\ bottom\ |\ home
.br
Sets the viewpoint to one of the predefined view angles.

.TP
.BI "\-\-camera\-angles " latitude " " longitude
Set the camera angles in degrees around the model.

.TP
.BI "\-\-camera\-position " x " " y " " z "  " tx " " ty " " tz "  " ux " " uy " " uz
Set the camera position, target and up vector using the \fIStudWorx\fR coordinate system.

.TP
.BI "\-\-camera\-position\-ldraw " x " " y " " z "  " tx " " ty " " tz "  " ux " " uy " " uz
Set the camera position, target and up vector using the \fILDraw\fR coordinate system.

.TP
\fB\-\-projection \fRperspective\ |\ orthographic
.br
Render images with a perspective or an orthographic projection.

.TP
.B \-\-transparent
Render images with a transparent background. Only PNG and GIF files keep
transparency, and GIF edges are hard; other formats are saved opaque with a warning.

.TP
.BI "\-\-field\-of\-view " degrees
Set the vertical field of view used to render images, under 180 degrees.

.TP
.BI "\-\-clip\-planes " near " " far
Set the near and far clipping planes used to render images (1 <= \fInear\fR < \fIfar\fR).

.TP
.B \-\-fade\-steps
Render parts from prior steps faded.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-fade\-steps
Do not render parts from prior steps faded.

.TP
.BI "\-\-fade\-color " color
Color to use for rendering faded parts. (#AARRGGBB where AA, RR, GG, and BB are hexadecimal values for alpha, red, green, and blue respectively.)

.TP
.B \-\-highlight
Highlight parts in the steps they appear.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-highlight
Do not highlight parts in the steps they appear.

.TP
.BI "\-\-highlight\-color " color
Color to use to highlight parts, (#AARRGGBB where AA, RR, GG, and BB are hexadecimal values for alpha, red, green, and blue respectively.)

.TP
\fB\-\-shading \fRwireframe\ |\ flat\ |\ default\ |\ full
.br
Select shading mode for rendering.

.TP
\fB\-\-lighting \fRstandard\ |\ studio\ |\ matte\ |\ toon
.br
Select the lighting style used by the default shading mode.

.TP
.BI "\-\-line\-width " width
Set the width of the edge lines.

.TP
.BI "\-\-antialiasing\-samples " count
Anti-aliasing sample size (1, 2, 4, or 8).

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-stud\-cylinder\-color
.br
Disable high contrast stud cylinder color.

.TP
\fB\-\-stud\-cylinder\-color\ \fI#AARRGGBB
.br
High contrast stud cylinder color.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-edge\-color
.br
Disable high contrast edge color.

.TP
\fB\-\-edge\-color\ \fI#AARRGGBB
.br
High contrast edge color.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-edge\-color\-black
.br
Disable high contrast edge color for black parts.

.TP
\fB\-\-edge\-color\-black\ \fI#AARRGGBB
.br
High contrast edge color for black parts.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-edge\-color\-dark
.br
Disable high contrast edge color for dark color parts.

.TP
\fB\-\-edge\-color\-dark\ \fI#AARRGGBB
.br
High contrast edge color for dark color parts.

.TP
\fB\-\-edge\-color\-automatic
.br
Enable automatically adjusted edge colors. The high contrast stud cylinder
and edge color options are ignored while it is set.

.TP
\fB\-\-edge\-contrast\ \fIfloat
.br
Set the edge color contrast, between 0.0 and 1.0. Needs automatic edge
colors, from \fB\-\-edge\-color\-automatic\fR or Preferences.

.TP
\fB\-\-edge\-light\-dark\ \fIfloat
.br
Set the value, between 0.0 and 1.0, that tells light colors from dark ones.
Needs automatic edge colors, from \fB\-\-edge\-color\-automatic\fR or Preferences.

.TP
\fB\-\-flatten \fR\fIoutfile.ldr\fR
.br
Replaces every submodel at all depths with its parts and saves the model, before any other export.

.TP
\fB\-\-undo \fR\fIoutfile.ldr\fR
.br
Undoes every command line edit and saves the model, to check that undo restores it.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-wavefront \fR[\fIoutfile.obj\fR]
.br
Exports the model to wavefront format.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-3ds \fR[\fIoutfile.3ds\fR]
.br
Exports the model to 3DS format.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-collada \fR[\fIoutfile.dae\fR]
.br
Exports the model to COLLADA DAE format. Transparent colors are written with opaque="A_ONE" while Mark COLLADA Transparency is on in Preferences.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-kmz \fR[\fIoutfile.kmz\fR]
.br
Exports the model to KMZ format.

.TP
\fB\-\-kmz\-geometry \fIall\fR|\fIvisible\fR
.br
Keeps every part, or flattens the model to the visible surfaces with one mesh per color, in KMZ exports.
Without it, the KMZ Geometry preference is used.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-csv \fR[\fIoutfile.csv\fR]
.br
Exports the list of parts used in CSV format.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-bricklink \fR[\fIoutfile.xml\fR]
.br
Exports the list of parts used in BrickLink XML format, ready for a BrickLink wanted list.
Part numbers and colors are translated through the BrickLink mapping file set in the preferences, or the bundled one when none is set.
Parts the library moved to a new number are listed under that number, and the exceptions file replaces the mapping of the parts it lists.

.TP
\fB\-\-bricklink\-condition \fIany\fR|\fInew\fR|\fIused\fR
.br
Sets the condition wanted in BrickLink exports.

.TP
\fB\-\-bricklink\-wanted\-list \fIid\fR|\fIurl\fR
.br
Sets the BrickLink wanted list the exported parts are added to, by its number or by the address of its wanted list page.
An address without a list number uses the main wanted list.

.TP
\fB\-\-bricklink\-notify
.br
Asks BrickLink to notify new listings of the exported parts.

.TP
\fB\-\-bricklink\-exceptions \fIfile\fR
.br
Sets the comma or tab separated file of parts and the BrickLink numbers that replace their mapping in BrickLink exports.
Without it the exceptions file set in the Export BrickLink dialog is used.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-html \fR[\fIpath\fR]
.br
Creates HTML instructions in a folder named after the model inside \fIpath\fR, starting at index.html.
With Single Page set in the Export HTML dialog, index.html scrolls through the Instructions window pages with #page-N and #step-N links and First, Previous, Next and Last Page arrows on the right, left or bottom edge, laid out for the shape chosen in Display and saved at twice the shown size. Background Color fills the step images, transparent when its alpha is zero, and Override Instructions Settings applies it, the Parts List choices and the Settings Overrides colors to the Single Page export.
Single Page cards round their corners like the Corner Radius of the step model box, and Edit Style Sheet replaces the CSS of the pages, with comments naming the feature of each block.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-povray \fR[\fIoutfile.pov\fR]
.br
Exports the model to POV-Ray format.

.TP
\fB\-\-render\-povray \fR[\fIoutfile.png\fR]
.br
Renders the model with POV-Ray 3.7 or newer into a PNG picture, using the POV-Ray window settings with the picture width, height and transparency from \fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-height\fR and \fB\-\-transparent\fR. POV-Ray is found in the Preferences path, the PATH, Flatpak or Snap.

.TP
\fB\-\-import\-settings \fIinfile.ini
.br
Imports the application settings and exits.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-settings \fIoutfile.ini
.br
Exports the application settings and exits.

.TP
\fB\-\-import\-keyboard\-shortcuts \fIinfile.txt
.br
Imports the keyboard shortcuts and exits.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-keyboard\-shortcuts \fIoutfile.txt
.br
Exports the keyboard shortcuts and exits.

.TP
\fB\-\-import\-mouse\-shortcuts \fIinfile.txt
.br
Imports the mouse shortcuts and exits.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-mouse\-shortcuts \fIoutfile.txt
.br
Exports the mouse shortcuts and exits.

.TP
\fB\-\-import\-categories \fIinfile.txt
.br
Imports the part categories and exits.

.TP
\fB\-\-export\-categories \fIoutfile.txt
.br
Exports the part categories and exits.

.TP
.BR \-v ",\ " \-\-version
Output version information and exit.

.TP
.BR \-h ",\ " \-\-help
Display this help message and exit.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
``LDRAW_DIRECTORY'' may be set to the parts library folder or archive, and
overrides the library set in the preferences. ``LDRAWDIR'' is read when
``LDRAW_DIRECTORY'' is not set. The same library is passed on to Blender.
.PP
When neither ``DISPLAY'' nor ``WAYLAND_DISPLAY'' is set, the save and export
options run without a display through the eglfs platform and EGL on the DRM
device, with software rendering when the GPU is in use by another session.
Set ``QT_QPA_PLATFORM'' to choose another platform.
.PP
``LDRAWDIR'' is also searched for the LGEO library used by POV-Ray renders.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
 $ studworx car.ldr \-i car.png \-w 640 \-\-height 480
.PP
This will start StudWorx, load the file "car.ldr", create a png called
"car.png" with a resolution of 640x480 and exit when done.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/StudWorx/StudWorx.conf
User preferences file
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/StudWorx/StudWorx/complete.zip
Parts library downloaded on the first start
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/StudWorx/StudWorx/lgeo
LGEO library used by POV-Ray renders

